.TH WIRESHARK 1 "December 2024" "Network Security" "Lab Commands"
.SH NAME
wireshark_lab \- Customized Wireshark display filters for lab analysis
.SH DESCRIPTION
Essential Wireshark display filters for quick packet analysis
(Lab Sheet 4: Part 1).
.SH DISPLAY FILTERS
.TP
.B All packets involving a specific IP
ip.addr == 192.168.56.101
.TP
.B HTTP traffic only
tcp.port == 80
.br
(or simply: http)
.TP
.B DNS traffic only
dns
.TP
.B Unencrypted FTP or Telnet
ftp or telnet
.TP
.B TCP retransmissions
tcp.analysis.retransmission
.TP
.B HTTP GET requests only
http.request.method == "GET"
.SH LAB CHALLENGES
.TP
.B Identify TCP flows (exercise 2)
Use: tcp.flags.syn==1 and tcp.flags.ack==0
.br
(Initial SYN packets)
.TP
.B Extract credentials (exercise 3)
Filter: telnet or ftp
.br
(Inspect raw payload in "Packet Details")
.TP
.B Detect suspicious activity (exercise 5)
Use filters:
.br
icmp
.br
tcp.analysis.flags
.SH AUTHOR
Exam preparation cheat-sheet.

